      ":question/id": "af8d7c5c-930c-59d3-b49e-ff7666f63383",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-346081",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=\\frac{\\pi x}{4},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
